description:
We present PageTML, an open-source, dependency-free JavaScript library that enables research-ers to create fully interactive psychological experiments and surveys using only HTML, CSS, and minimal JavaScript. By extending standard HTML with lightweight custom elements (e.g., , , , etc.), PageTML eliminates the need for complex frameworks while preserving full control over the browser’s document object model. Core features include:
•	slide-based sequencing with configurable navigation keys, auto-advance timers (maxms), and millisecond-level timing via setTimeout; Automatic data logging for any element with a name attribute, with one-click export to JSON or CSV via  or ;
•	feedback-rich error messaging for real-time status (pending, success, error);
•	dynamic content insertion (jsfill, idfill) and flexible trial ordering (shuffle or pseudoshuf-fle for a given tolerance);
•	multi-session workflow via subject and session codes as well as agendas which allow nav-igation through multiple URLs while preserving participant information, making previous experiments reusable;
•	additional backend logic for data upload and checks are implemented in PHP.
Designed for accessibility to novice programmers, PageTML prioritizes readability, reusability, and extensibility: custom JavaScript can be inserted anywhere without interfering with library logic. Example paradigms (Number comparison task, surveys) are provided in the repository. Version 0.3 is released under the MIT license at https://github.com/RomanJJa/PageTML. Future releases will add adaptive logic, WebGazer integration, and multilingual UI. PageTML lowers barriers to online data collection, enabling rapid prototyping, classroom use, and large-scale de-ployment in psychological science.
